    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/87CB6D0141B0DF4C2F65FFEBD183CE63/jobs/205919": {
      "title": "Director of the Mental Health Counseling Program",
      "description": "Director of the Mental Health Counseling Program You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Director of the Mental Health Counseling Program Barton College - Wilson, NC 27893 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Apply Description The School of Health Sciences at Barton College invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track Director of the Master of Science in Clinical Mental Health Counseling (CMHC) program, with an anticipated start date of January 2026. The Director will provide visionary and strategic leadership in developing, implementing, and overseeing Barton College’s new CMHC program. Key responsibilities include guiding the program through the CACREP accreditation process, ensuring compliance with SACSCOC standards, coordinating curriculum design and delivery, managing clinical training partnerships, recruiting and mentoring faculty, and supporting student learning and success. The successful candidate will teach graduate-level counseling courses, oversee program operations, and collaborate closely with the Dean of the School of Health Sciences and other campus leaders to align the program with the mission of Barton College and the evolving needs of the counseling profession. The Director will also cultivate strong community and clinical partnerships, engage in professional scholarship and development, and contribute to the College’s shared governance and service activities. The successful candidate will demonstrate a commitment to excellence in teaching. Qualifications Required Education, Skills, and Experience: Doctorate (Ph.D. or Ed.D.) in Counselor Education and Supervision from a CACREP-accredited program Eligibility for licensure as a Licensed Clinical Mental Health Counselor (LCMHC) in the state of North Carolina (required) Strong communication and interpersonal skills with a commitment to working with students and colleagues of diverse backgrounds Record of teaching excellence, particularly across multiple delivery formats (face-to-face, hybrid, and online) Preferred Qualifications: Demonstrated experience with CACREP accreditation Prior administrative or leadership experience in a counseling program Familiarity with SACSCOC or other regional accreditation processes Experience in curriculum design and program implementation across diverse instructional modalities Barton College is an equal employment opportunity employer committed to a diverse faculty, staff, and student body and welcomes all applicants. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Any claims of discrimination for Title IX or otherwise should be directed to our Director of Title IX & Campus Relations, Corey Coley, at P.O. Box 5000, Wilson, NC 27893, or at 252-399-6319 or cocoley@barton.edu. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/87CB6D0141B0DF4C2F65FFEBD183CE63/jobs/211485": {
      "title": "Adjunct- School of Health Sciences",
      "description": "Adjunct- School of Health Sciences You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Adjunct- School of Health Sciences Barton College - Wilson, NC 27893 Apply Apply Description Adjunct faculty are hired on a semester-by-semester basis to support the College’s academic mission through quality instruction, student engagement, and academic excellence. Courses may be offered in-person, online, or in a hybrid format, depending on departmental needs. Teaching Opportunities Adjunct teaching opportunities may be available in the following subject areas: Biology Physics Exercise Science Psychology Chemistry Nursing Kinesiology General Science Essential Duties and Responsibilities Adjunct faculty responsibilities include, but are not limited to: Teach assigned courses in accordance with approved course syllabi and learning outcomes Develop and deliver engaging instruction that supports student success Maintain a classroom environment conducive to learning Provide timely evaluation and feedback on student assignments and assessments Maintain accurate records of attendance, grades, and course documentation Submit final grades by published deadlines Communicate regularly with students and respond to inquiries in a timely manner Utilize the College’s learning management system (LMS) and instructional technology as required Maintain professionalism and comply with College policies and procedures Participate in required training, orientation, and meetings as applicable Qualifications Required Qualifications Master’s degree in the discipline or a closely related field from an accredited institution Ability to teach at the college level with strong communication skills Commitment to supporting diverse learners and maintaining academic standards Preferred Qualifications Prior teaching experience in higher education Experience teaching online or hybrid courses Professional experience in the discipline area Experience using an LMS (Canvas, Blackboard, Moodle, etc.) Doctorate in the discipline or related field (where applicable) Ability to work evenings and/or weekends as needed based on course scheduling Successful completion of background check and employment verification Before submitting your application, please be sure to indicate the subject for which you are applying within the School. Barton College is an equal employment opportunity employer committed to a diverse faculty, staff, and student body and welcomes all applicants. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Any claims of discrimination for Title IX or otherwise should be directed to our Director of Title IX & Campus Relations, Corey Coley, at P.O. Box 5000, Wilson, NC 27893, or at 252-399-6319 or c ocoley@barton.edu . Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
