      "title": "Adjunct- School of Arts/Humanities & School of Education/Social Sciences",
      "description": "Adjunct- School of Arts/Humanities & School of Education/Social Sciences You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Adjunct- School of Arts/Humanities & School of Education/Social Sciences Barton College - Wilson, NC 27893 Apply Apply Description Adjunct faculty are hired on a semester-by-semester basis to support the College’s academic mission through quality instruction, student engagement, and academic excellence. Courses may be offered in-person, online, or in a hybrid format, depending on departmental needs. Teaching Opportunities Adjunct teaching opportunities may be available in the following subject areas: English/College Writing/First-year Composition Art Appreciation Mathematics Mass Communications Spanish Criminal Justice Education Essential Duties and Responsibilities Adjunct faculty responsibilities include, but are not limited to: Teach assigned courses in accordance with approved course syllabi and learning outcomes Develop and deliver engaging instruction that supports student success Maintain a classroom environment conducive to learning Provide timely evaluation and feedback on student assignments and assessments Maintain accurate records of attendance, grades, and course documentation Submit final grades by published deadlines Communicate regularly with students and respond to inquiries in a timely manner Utilize the College’s learning management system (LMS) and instructional technology as required Maintain professionalism and comply with College policies and procedures Participate in required training, orientation, and meetings as applicable Qualifications Required Qualifications Master’s degree in the discipline or a closely related field from an accredited institution Ability to teach at the college level with strong communication skills Commitment to supporting diverse learners and maintaining academic standards Preferred Qualifications Prior teaching experience in higher education Experience teaching online or hybrid courses Professional experience in the discipline area Experience using an LMS (Canvas, Blackboard, Moodle, etc.) Doctorate in the discipline or related field (where applicable) Ability to work evenings and/or weekends as needed based on course scheduling Successful completion of background check and employment verification Before submitting your application, please be sure to indicate the subject for which you are applying within the School. Barton College is an equal employment opportunity employer committed to a diverse faculty, staff, and student body and welcomes all applicants. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Any claims of discrimination for Title IX or otherwise should be directed to our Director of Title IX & Campus Relations, Corey Coley, at P.O. Box 5000, Wilson, NC 27893, or at 252-399-6319 or c ocoley@barton.edu . Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
