    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/87CB6D0141B0DF4C2F65FFEBD183CE63/jobs/219210": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Criminology and Criminal Justice",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Criminology and Criminal Justice You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Assistant Professor of Criminology and Criminal Justice Barton College - Wilson, NC 27893 Apply Apply Description Barton College is seeking candidates for a full-time tenure-track Assistant Professor of Criminology and Criminal Justice Sciences with an anticipated start date of January 4, 2027. The successful candidate will lead a range of Criminology courses at all levels of undergraduate and graduate course work, with a mix of seated and online/hybrid courses. Candidates must demonstrate a commitment to teaching students in a liberal arts setting. Additional responsibilities include academic advising, student recruitment, maintaining a program of active student engagement, meaningful participation in the life of the School of Education & Social Sciences and Barton College, and a commitment to active contributions in the profession. These contributions may include mentoring of student projects and development of pedagogy that engages students and fosters deep learning. Essential Functions. Teach up to 24 (twenty-four) credit hours annually of undergraduate plus graduate coursework. Sustain currency and relevancy through professional engagement and/or research related to professional background and experience. Mentor and advise students. Serve as an active faculty member of the Barton College School of Education & Social Sciences. Support student recruitment including participation at on-campus open houses. Display strong communication and interpersonal skills with a commitment to working with students and colleagues of diverse backgrounds. Work Environment. Work is performed in classrooms, offices, and virtual environments, including contact with students, faculty, staff, parents, service providers, and vendors. Qualifications A Ph.D. or ABD in the field of Criminology and Criminal Justice Sciences who is qualified to teach both undergraduate and graduate courses. Special interests and experience in teaching other subjects compatible with the Criminology and Criminal Justice Sciences Program and the needs of the College will be considered during the candidate assessment process. A demonstrated ability to deliver applied learning experiences. Demonstration of excellence in teaching. Ability to lead a wide range of Criminology/Criminal Justice Sciences courses. Under the direction of the dean, develop curriculum for new programs and curricular revisions. Collaborative disposition with a commitment to service. Proficiency in oral presentation skills, planning, and organizing of course objectives. Barton College is an equal employment opportunity employer committed to a diverse faculty, staff, and student body and welcomes all applicants. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Any claims of discrimination for Title IX or otherwise should be directed to our Director of Title IX & Campus Relations, Corey Coley, at P.O. Box 5000, Wilson, NC 27893, or at 252-399-6319 or c ocoley@barton.edu . Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/87CB6D0141B0DF4C2F65FFEBD183CE63/jobs/222697": {
      "title": "Adjunct- School of Business & Innovation",
      "description": "Adjunct- School of Business & Innovation You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Adjunct- School of Business & Innovation Barton College - Wilson, NC 27893 Apply Apply Description Adjunct faculty are hired on a semester-by-semester basis to support the College’s academic mission through quality instruction, student engagement, and academic excellence. Courses may be offered in-person, online, or in a hybrid format, depending on departmental needs. Teaching Opportunities Adjunct teaching opportunities may be available in the following subject areas: Accounting Marketing Management Economics Operations IT/MIS Finance AI Sport Management Healthcare Administration Essential Duties and Responsibilities Adjunct faculty responsibilities include, but are not limited to: Teach assigned courses in accordance with approved course syllabi and learning outcomes Develop and deliver engaging instruction that supports student success Maintain a classroom environment conducive to learning Provide timely evaluation and feedback on student assignments and assessments Maintain accurate records of attendance, grades, and course documentation Submit final grades by published deadlines Communicate regularly with students and respond to inquiries in a timely manner Utilize the College’s learning management system (LMS) and instructional technology as required Maintain professionalism and comply with College policies and procedures Participate in required training, orientation, and meetings as applicable Qualifications Required Qualifications Master’s degree in discipline or a closely related field from an accredited institution Ability to teach at the college level with strong communication skills Commitment to supporting diverse learners and maintaining academic standards Preferred Qualifications Prior teaching experience in higher education Experience teaching online or hybrid courses Professional experience in the discipline area Experience using an LMS (Canvas, Blackboard, Moodle, etc.) Doctorate in discipline or related field (where applicable) Ability to work evenings and/or weekends as needed based on course scheduling Successful completion of background check and employment verification Before submitting your application, please be sure to indicate the subject for which you are applying within the School. Barton College is an equal employment opportunity employer committed to a diverse faculty, staff, and student body and welcomes all applicants. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Any claims of discrimination for Title IX or otherwise should be directed to our Director of Title IX & Campus Relations, Corey Coley, at P.O. Box 5000, Wilson, NC 27893, or at 252-399-6319 or c ocoley@barton.edu . Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
