    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/87CB6D0141B0DF4C2F65FFEBD183CE63/jobs/223843": {
      "title": "Director of Development",
      "description": "Director of Development You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Director of Development Barton College - Wilson, NC 27893 Apply Apply Description Summary: Reporting to the Assistant Vice President of Development, the Director of Development is responsible for executing annual giving strategies, managing a portfolio of lead annual and mid-major donors, and overseeing stewardship activities that support donor retention and growth. This role is a key contributor to the College’s annual fund performance and plays an active role in advancing the donor pipeline through consistent outreach, thoughtful stewardship, and campaign execution, contributing to a team-based fundraising approach in which all Advancement staff support the College’s philanthropic goals. Essential Functions: Responsible for the management of Barton’s development efforts as it relates to annual giving strategies focused on the whole donor cycle for our donors, alumni, friends, employees, parents, students, and companies. - Execute annual giving strategies across constituencies. Design, implement, and manage all appeal campaigns throughout the fiscal year, including fall, year-end, fiscal year-end, and monthly anniversary appeals. This work will also include campaigns for specialty groups on campus, such as the Bulldog Club and Cultural Arts. - Support and implement peer-to-peer digital fundraising campaigns, including Clash of the Bulldogs in the fall and Giving Day in the spring. - Manage a portfolio of lead annual and mid-major donors, utilizing moves management strategies including identification, cultivation, solicitation, stewardship, and renewal. - Lead stewardship efforts for all donors, including thank you strategies, Quarterly Impact reporting, and donor recognition initiatives and events. - Assist in the development and execution of a comprehensive annual fund plan and solicitation calendar. - Partner with marketing and communications to support fundraising appeals, messaging, and campaign assets. - Track and report on fundraising performance throughout the fiscal year, including donor participation, retention, and campaign results - Maintain accurate donor records using Blackbaud Raiser’s Edge NXT and other systems. - Identify and help qualify prospects to support the major gift pipeline. - Manage student workers – currently two team members – to ensure this department’s success. Other Responsibilities: Assist as needed in all fundraising programs and activities of Barton College, and perform other duties as assigned. Provide professional, quality customer service to donors, alumni, volunteers, staff, and other contacts. Qualifications Required Experience: Bachelor’s degree required, and advance degree or CFRE preferred. Minimum of 5 years of development experience including demonstrated success in individual giving, corporate giving, alumni giving, volunteer management, and special events fundraising and management. Ability to manage team members. Excellent written and verbal communication skills and the ability to work effectively with diverse constituencies, as well as good judgement and ability to handle confidential / sensitive information with discretion. Ability to manage multiple and competing priorities and meet deadlines in a dynamic environment. Experience with moves management including prospect identification, cultivation, solicitation, and stewardship. Experience with digital fundraising, peer-to-peer fundraising, managing website promotions and giving days. Experience with fundraising data management systems; Blackbaud Raiser’s Edge NXT is highly desirable. Optimistic attitude, self-motivated, and eager to be part of an emerging team. Barton College is an equal employment opportunity employer committed to a diverse faculty, staff, and student body and welcomes all applicants. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Any claims of discrimination for Director of Title IX and Campus Relations or otherwise should be directed to our Title IX Coordinator, Corey Coley, at P.O. Box 5000, Wilson, NC 27893, or at 252-399-6319 or cocoley@barton.edu. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/87CB6D0141B0DF4C2F65FFEBD183CE63/jobs/231199": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Business Analytics & Applied Artificial Intelligence",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Business Analytics & Applied Artificial Intelligence You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Assistant Professor of Business Analytics & Applied Artificial Intelligence Barton College - Wilson, NC 27893 Apply Apply Description Barton College is seeking candidates for a full-time tenure-track Assistant Professor of Business Analytics & Applied Artificial Intelligence with an anticipated start date of January 4, 2027. The successful candidate will lead a range of courses in the Business Analytics & Applied Artificial Intelligence program, with a mix of seated and online/hybrid courses. Candidates must demonstrate a commitment to teaching students in a liberal arts setting. Additional responsibilities include academic advising, student recruitment, maintaining a program of active student engagement, meaningful participation in the life of the School of Business & Innovation and Barton College, and a commitment to active contributions in the profession. These contributions may include mentoring student projects, development of pedagogy that engages students and fosters deep learning, and applied projects that connect analytics and AI to real-world business problems. Essential Functions. Teach up to 24 (twenty-four) credit hours annually of coursework in Business Analytics & Applied Artificial Intelligence (BA&AAI). Sustain currency and relevancy through professional engagement and industry partnerships. Mentor and advise students. Serve as an active faculty member of the Barton College School of Business Analytics & Innovation. Support student recruitment including participation at on-campus open houses and development of program promotion collateral. Display strong communication and interpersonal skills with a commitment to working with students and colleagues of diverse backgrounds. Qualifications Demonstration of excellence in teaching. Ability to lead a wide range of Business Analytics & Applied Artificial Intelligence courses ( e.g., applied AI, AI ethics, business analytics, data visualization, and predictive modeling). Under the direction of the Dean, ability to develop curriculum for new programs including certificates and micro-credentials. Collaborative disposition with a commitment to service. Proficiency in oral presentation skills, planning, and organizing of course objectives. Demonstrated comfort applying artificial intelligence tools and techniques in business and decision-making contexts. The successful candidate will be an innovative individual with: A terminal degree (Ph.D. or DBA preferred; ABD considered) in Business Analytics, Data Science, Applied Artificial Intelligence, Information Systems, Statistics, or a closely related field. A demonstrated ability to deliver applied learning experiences including hands-on projects with analytics tools ( e.g. , Python, R, SQL, Tableau/Bower BI) and AI frameworks. Special interests and experiences in teaching other subjects compatible with the BA&AAI program and the needs of the School of Business & Innovation will be considered. Barton College is an equal employment opportunity employer committed to a diverse faculty, staff, and student body and welcomes all applicants. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Any claims of discrimination for Title IX or otherwise should be directed to our Director of Title IX & Campus Relations, Corey Coley, at P.O. Box 5000, Wilson, NC 27893, or at 252-399-6319 or cocoley@barton.edu . Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/87CB6D0141B0DF4C2F65FFEBD183CE63/jobs/238036": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Athletic Trainer",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate Athletic Trainer You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Assistant/Associate Athletic Trainer Apply Apply Description The Assistant/Associate Athletic Trainer works under the supervision of the Associate Athletic Director for Sports Medicine and supervises the care of student-athletes competing in the College’s athletic programs. The Assistant/Associate Athletic Trainer is responsible for the prevention, evaluation, management of injuries within the College’s comprehensive sports medicine program. Essential Functions: Prevention of athletic injuries and illness. Evaluation and treatment of athletic injuries. Athletic training administrative duties Assist with coordination and scheduling of medical coverage for home and away competitions. Recordkeeping and documentation. Work with doctors and other allied health professionals to deliver care to student-athletes Other Areas: Other duties assigned by the Associate Athletic Director for Sports Medicine and Director of Athletics. Qualifications Desired Education, Skills, and Experience: Master’s degree preferred, Bachelor’s degree in appropriate area of specialization required.  Three to five years professional experience and/or training; or equivalent combination of education and experience.  Certified by the Board of Certification (BOC), State Athletic Training Licensure and First Aid/CPR. Possession of or ability to obtain a valid North Carolina Driver’s license.  Knowledge and experience of insurance policies and procedures, submitting claims and explanation of benefits. Basic knowledge of NCAA regulations. Strong oral and written skills; excellent interpersonal and teamwork skills, and adequate computer skills. High ethical standards and ability to work with a diverse faculty, staff, students and other publics. Ability to maintain a high level of confidentiality. Barton College is an equal employment opportunity employer committed to a diverse faculty, staff, and student body and welcomes all applicants. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Any claims of discrimination for Title IX or otherwise should be directed to our Director of Title IX & Campus Relations, Corey Coley, at P.O. Box 5000, Wilson, NC 27893, or at 252-399-6319 or cocoley@barton.edu . Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/87CB6D0141B0DF4C2F65FFEBD183CE63/jobs/242538": {
      "title": "Assistant Lacrosse Coach/Athletic Associate",
      "description": "Assistant Lacrosse Coach/Athletic Associate You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Assistant Lacrosse Coach/Athletic Associate Barton College - Wilson, NC 27893 Apply Apply Description This individual will assist the head coach in all aspects of running the day-to-day operations of the sport program. It is his/her responsibility to foster and encourage goals of student-athletes, stress the elements of sportsmanship and fair play and do so within the mission of Barton College, Conference Carolinas and the NCAA. Note: This job description indicates in general the nature and levels of work, knowledge, skills, abilities and other essential functions (as covered under the Americans with Disabilities Act) expected of an incumbent. It is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities required of an incumbent. An incumbent may be asked to perform other duties as required. Essential Functions: • To assist the men's lacrosse program according to all College, Conference Carolinas, and NCAA rules, regulations, guidelines, and standards for financial aid, eligibility, and recruiting. • To operate within the men's lacrosse team budget and follow purchasing and spending guidelines as set by the College. • To successfully pass the NCAA Division II University program. (yearly) • To recruit quality student-athletes. • To assist with student-athlete eligibility certification and completion of forms and medical exams, and provide NCAA reports to the Compliance Office as required, report any NCAA rules violations, injuries or accidents involving student-athletes, and misconduct of student-athletes. • To assist with the planning and execution of practices, individual skill development, game preparation, scouting, film review, and game-day coaching responsibilities as assigned by the Head Men's Lacrosse Coach. • To work, communicate, and develop rapport with students, parents, alumni, faculty/staff, and administration and to engage in public relations activities and to promote Barton College and the men's lacrosse program in a positive manner. • To perform any additional duties that may be assigned by the Head Men's Lacrosse Coach. Other Areas: • To perform any additional duties that may be assigned by the Director of Athletics. This is a general description for all assistant coaches. These distinct areas of assignment may be advertised separately in recruiting ads/documents separate from the job description as needed. Work Environment: The work environment is variable depending on athletic event settings specific to the sport managed. Internal office work is also required. The noise level in the work environment is usually moderate but occasionally high depending upon student population, event attendees and activities involved. The employee is regularly exposed to outdoor weather conditions and may be exposed to bodily fluids and blood borne pathogens. Physical Demands: The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job. This is largely a physically active role requiring the employee to have the ability to teach proper techniques to students and have the requisite skills needed for athletic participation. Therefore the physical abilities required include: the ability to walk, run, jump, stretch, stand, sit, talk, hear, using hands for fine manipulation, to handle or feel and reach with hands and arms using a keyboard and video display terminal. The employee is occasionally required to stoop, kneel, crouch or crawl and must regularly lift and/or move up to 25 pounds and occasionally up to 100 pounds. The employee may also have to climb stairs or ladders and specific vision requirements include the ability to see up close, distantly, adjust his/her focus and have adequate peripheral vision for the position. Qualifications Desired Education, Skills, and Experience : Masters degree preferred, Bachelors and/or Associates (AA) required. Collegiate lacrosse playing experience and coaching experience preferred. Must be willing to obtain certifications in CPR/First Aid/AED and be willing to obtain other certifications as needed. Possession of or ability to obtain a valid North Carolina Driver’s license. Experience and knowledge of lacrosse training with the ability to improve individual techniques/skills and game strategy. Experience and knowledge of NCAA regulations. Strong oral and written skills; excellent interpersonal and teamwork skills, and adequate computer skills. High ethical standards and ability to work with a diverse faculty, staff, students and other publics. Ability to maintain a high level of confidentiality. Barton College is an equal employment opportunity employer committed to a diverse faculty, staff, and student body and welcomes all applicants. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Any claims of discrimination for Title IX or otherwise should be directed to our Title IX Coordinator, Corey Coley, at P.O. Box 5000, Wilson, NC 27893, or at 252-399-6319 or cocoley@barton.edu. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/87CB6D0141B0DF4C2F65FFEBD183CE63/jobs/244450": {
      "title": "Facilities Custodial Worker",
      "description": "Facilities   Custodial Worker You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Facilities   Custodial Worker Apply Apply Description Barton College currently has an opening for a Custodial Worker responsible for cleaning assigned buildings. Regular duties include vacuuming classrooms and offices, cleaning restrooms, emptying trash, wiping and dusting vertical and horizontal surfaces, and performing annual maintenance such as waxing floors and cleaning carpets. May require working nights and/or weekends in support of college events as needed. Note: This job description indicates in general the nature and levels of work, knowledge, skills, abilities and other essential functions (as covered under the Americans with Disabilities Act) expected of an incumbent.  It is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties, or responsibilities required of an incumbent.  An incumbent may be asked to perform other duties as required. Essential Functions Trash Duty and General Cleaning (25%) Empty waste receptacles Polish furniture Clean chalkboards/whiteboards Disinfect horizontal and vertical surfaces Organize and stock supply closet Floor and Carpet Care (25%) Dust, mop, and apply finish to various types of floors Vacuum and shampoo various types of carpets Restroom Cleaning (25%) Clean, sanitize, and/or disinfect restrooms, showers, bathtubs, sinks using prescribed schedules, methods, and procedures Clean and disinfect all dispensers, fixtures, and mirrors Refill toilet tissue, paper towel, and soap dispensers Sweep and mop tile floors Clean and disinfect partitions and doors Utility Cleaning (20%) Operate various types of powered equipment such as electric strippers, buffers, burnishers, power washers, and vacuums Request cleaning supplies as needed Sweep and mop stairs as needed Haul trash to dumpsters Sweep and mop entrances of buildings Clean windows and glass Mop and scrub hard surface floors Move and transport furniture to different locations Set up rooms in a timely manner for meetings and special events Replace light bulbs, fluorescent tubes, vacuum belts, and bags Other Duties as Assigned (5%) Complete req uired forms and paperwork as needed Report broken and malfunctioning equipment to supervisor Request cleaning supplies Work Environment This job requires working with and around hazardous building materials and solvents; frequent lifting; frequent use of ladders; and exposure to hot and cold temperatures when working outside. Physical Demands The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job. This is largely a physical role requiring moderate physical strength. Requires the ability to lift boxes and trash bags up to 50lbs. Perform custodial tasks including mopping, sweeping, vacuuming, washing windows, and cleaning restrooms. Qualifications Desired Education, Skills, and Experience Graduation from high school or equivalent education OR 12 months of general work experience. Ability to: read labels and directions on cleaning agents and equipment follow oral and written instructions read and understand written instructions, directions, and assembly schematics communicate effectively both verbally and in writing learn new methods of cleaning establish and maintain effective working relationships with supervisors, employees, vendors, and the general public perform basic maintenance on custodial equipment such as changing belts, brushes, and replacing bags operate various powered equipment used to scrub, strip, apply finish, vacuum, polish, burnish, and buff various types of floors General knowledge of: practices related to custodial services environmental health and safety practices applicable to custodial services such as handling hazardous materials and awareness of asbestos and blood-borne pathogens cleaning agents, materials and equipment used in custodial functions safe and proper methods of using/mixing cleaning chemicals proper care and cleaning of assigned areas Barton College is an equal employment opportunity employer committed to a diverse faculty, staff, and student body and welcomes all applicants. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Any claims of discrimination for Title IX or otherwise should be directed to our Director of Title IX and Campus Relations, Corey Coley, at P.O. Box 5000, Wilson, NC 27893, or at 252-399-6319. or cocoley@barton.edu. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/87CB6D0141B0DF4C2F65FFEBD183CE63/jobs/246005": {
      "title": "Assistant Athletic Director for Logistics",
      "description": "Assistant Athletic Director for Logistics You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Assistant Athletic Director for Logistics Barton College - Wilson, NC 27893 Apply Apply Description The Assistant Athletic Director is a key member of the intercollegiate athletics leadership team and supports the Director of Athletics in the administration and daily operation of the department. The position provides leadership and oversight in student-athlete engagement, team travel, ticketing and game-day operations, and other administrative functions that support a successful student-athlete experience. The successful candidate will be highly organized, collaborative, service-oriented, and comfortable working in a fast-paced small-college athletics environment. This position requires frequent interaction with student-athletes, coaches, administrators, campus partners, vendors, transportation providers, and conference representatives. Essential Responsibilities Team Travel ● Coordinate and oversee team travel arrangements for athletic contests, tournaments, championships, and other approved department activities. ● Develop travel itineraries and communicate travel details to coaches, teams, transportation providers, and appropriate campus personnel. ● Coordinate transportation, lodging, meals, and other travel-related services. ● Work with coaches to establish travel plans that meet institutional policies, budget parameters, and competitive schedules. ● Maintain accurate records of travel arrangements, confirmations, invoices, and related documentation. ● Establish and maintain relationships with hotels, bus companies, rental agencies, and other travel vendors. ● Assist with emergency or last-minute travel changes and provide appropriate support to teams while traveling. ● Monitor travel expenses and work with the Director of Athletics and appropriate campus offices to ensure responsible use of departmental resources. ● Coordinate championship and postseason travel as assigned. ● Assist with travel-related risk management and ensure appropriate procedures are followed. ● Communicate changes to schedules, transportation, lodging, and other travel arrangements in a timely manner. Ticketing & Game-Day Operations ● Oversee the athletics department's ticketing operations for designated home athletic events. ● Establish and maintain ticket prices, complimentary ticket procedures, season ticket programs, and applicable admission policies in coordination with the Director of Athletics. ● Manage ticket sales and distribution through the department's designated ticketing platform. ● Coordinate ticketing operations with campus partners, visiting teams, conference representatives, officials, vendors, and event staff. ● Recruit, train, schedule, and supervise game-day ticketing and admissions personnel. ● Develop game-day procedures for ticket sales, cash handling, digital ticketing, will-call, complimentary admissions, and event entry. ● Reconcile ticket revenue and provide appropriate financial documentation following events. ● Monitor ticket sales and attendance trends and make recommendations to increase attendance and fan engagement. ● Coordinate special ticketing arrangements for students, faculty, staff, alumni, donors, community members, and special guests. ● Assist with game-day hospitality and VIP experiences as assigned. ● Ensure ticketing and admission procedures provide a welcoming, professional experience for fans and guests. ● Assist with troubleshooting ticketing issues before and during athletic events. Athletics Administration ● Assist the Director of Athletics with the daily administration and operation of the athletics department. ● Assist the Associate Athletic Director with the SAAC. ● Support department-wide policies, procedures, strategic initiatives, and operational projects. ● Assist with scheduling, facilities, personnel, purchasing, budgeting, compliance, and event management as assigned. ● Serve as an administrator on duty for designated home athletic contests. ● Assist coaches and athletics staff with operational needs and problem resolution. ● Participate in athletics department meetings and institutional committees as assigned. ● Assist with NCAA, conference, and institutional reporting and compliance responsibilities. ● Maintain accurate records and documentation related to assigned areas of responsibility. ● Assist with the development and implementation of departmental policies and procedures. ● Represent the athletics department professionally with students, families, alumni, fans, campus personnel, opposing institutions, conference representatives, and community partners. Student-Athlete Experience ● Promote an inclusive, supportive, and positive environment for all student-athletes. ● Assist in identifying opportunities to improve the overall student-athlete experience. ● Collaborate with campus partners in Student Affairs, Academic Affairs, Health Services, Counseling, Admissions, Advancement, and other areas to support student-athlete success. ● Assist with student-athlete orientation, recognition, awards, and engagement programs. ● Help communicate important departmental information and resources to student-athletes. ● Support initiatives designed to develop leadership, citizenship, career readiness, and life skills among student-athletes. Qualifications Desired Education, Skills, and Experience: Required ● Bachelor's degree from an accredited college or university. ● Experience in intercollegiate athletics, athletic administration, event management, student affairs, or a related field. ● Strong organizational and time-management skills. ● Excellent written and verbal communication skills. ● Demonstrated ability to work effectively with student-athletes, coaches, administrators, and external partners. ● Strong attention to detail and ability to manage multiple priorities simultaneously. ● Proficiency with standard office and technology applications. ● Ability to work evenings, weekends, and holidays as required by the athletics schedule. Preferred ● Master's degree in athletic administration, sport management, higher education, business administration, or a related field. ● Previous experience advising or coordinating a Student-Athlete Advisory Council. ● Experience coordinating intercollegiate team travel. ● Experience with athletic ticketing and event-management software. ● Experience with NCAA or conference rules and regulations. ● Experience working in a small-college athletics environment. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities The successful candidate should possess: ● Strong leadership, interpersonal, and relationship-building skills. ● Exceptional organizational and logistical abilities. ● Ability to anticipate problems and develop practical solutions. ● Strong customer-service orientation. ● Ability to communicate effectively with diverse constituencies. ● Ability to handle confidential and sensitive information appropriately. ● Ability to manage financial and operational responsibilities with accuracy and accountability. ● Ability to remain calm and effective in high-pressure or rapidly changing situations. ● Willingness to be a hands-on member of a small athletics department and assist wherever needed. Work Environment The position is based in a dynamic intercollegiate athletics environment. Regular evening and weekend work is required based on athletic contests, team travel, SAAC activities, championships, and special events. The position may require occasional overnight travel. Performance Expectations Performance in this position will be evaluated based on the successful administration of assigned responsibilities, including: ● Effective leadership and engagement of the Student-Athlete Advisory Council. ● Accurate, efficient, and cost-effective coordination of team travel. ● Professional and reliable management of ticketing and admissions operations. ● Positive student-athlete and customer experiences. ● Effective game-day and event operations. ● Compliance with institutional, conference, and NCAA policies. ● Strong communication and collaboration with coaches, student-athletes, campus partners, and external constituents. ● Demonstrated initiative in improving athletics operations and the student-athlete experience. Barton College is an equal employment opportunity employer committed to a diverse faculty, staff, and student body and welcomes all applicants. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Any claims of discrimination for Title IX or otherwise should be directed to our Title IX Coordinator, Corey Coley, at P.O. Box 5000, Wilson, NC 27893, or at 252-399-6319 or cocoley @barton.edu . Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/87CB6D0141B0DF4C2F65FFEBD183CE63/jobs/246001": {
      "title": "Assistant Athletic Director for External Relations",
      "description": "Assistant Athletic Director for External Relations You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Assistant Athletic Director for External Relations Barton College - Wilson, NC 27893 Apply Apply Description The Assistant Athletic Director for External Relations serves as a key member of the athletics leadership team and is responsible for strengthening the department’s relationships with alumni, donors, parents, community partners, corporate sponsors, media, and other external constituents. This position leads efforts to enhance the visibility, reputation, and financial support of the college’s athletics program. At a small college, this is a highly collaborative and hands-on role. The Assistant Athletic Director will work across athletics, advancement, communications, admissions, student affairs, and campus leadership to tell the story of the institution’s student-athletes and create meaningful opportunities for engagement and support. Essential Responsibilities ● Develop and implement a comprehensive external relations strategy for the athletics department. ● Build and maintain strong relationships with alumni, donors, parents, fans, community leaders, businesses, and corporate partners. ● Assist with athletics fundraising initiatives, including annual giving, major gifts, special campaigns, and athletic-specific fundraising events ● Identify and cultivate corporate sponsorship opportunities and develop mutually beneficial partnerships with local and regional businesses. ● Coordinate athletics alumni and donor engagement activities, including reunions, recognition events, receptions, and special events. ● Work closely with the college’s Advancement and Communications teams to align athletics fundraising, marketing, and engagement efforts with institutional priorities. ● Develop compelling stories and communications highlighting student-athletes, coaches, teams, academic achievements, community service, and institutional accomplishments. ● Oversee or assist with athletics social media, digital communications, newsletters, email campaigns, and other external-facing communications. ● Serve as a public-facing representative of the athletics department at campus, alumni, community, and athletic events. ● Assist with planning and execution of home athletic events, including special guests, sponsors, donor hospitality, recognition activities, and promotional initiatives. ● Develop strategies to increase attendance, fan engagement, school spirit, and community participation at athletic events. ● Coordinate sponsor recognition and fulfillment, including signage, digital assets, announcements, hospitality, and promotional opportunities. ● Assist with athletics marketing and branding initiatives to increase awareness of the college and its athletic programs. ● Maintain accurate records of external contacts, prospects, sponsors, donors, and engagement activities in appropriate institutional databases. ● Collaborate with coaches and athletics staff to identify opportunities for alumni, donor, and community engagement. ● Assist with athletics department publications, annual reports, presentations, fundraising materials, and promotional campaigns. ● Represent the college and athletics department professionally at conferences, community events, alumni functions, and other external engagements. ● Support the Director of Athletics with special projects and strategic initiatives. ● Perform other duties as assigned. Fundraising & Development A significant component of the position will be helping the athletics department develop a sustainable culture of philanthropy. Responsibilities may include: ● Developing an annual athletics fundraising plan. ● Identifying and researching prospective donors and sponsors. ● Cultivating relationships with athletics alumni and friends of the college. ● Supporting major gift and annual giving initiatives. ● Creating athletics-focused fundraising campaigns and giving opportunities. ● Assisting with donor stewardship and recognition. ● Organizing fundraising events and giving-day initiatives. ● Working with coaches to develop appropriate fundraising strategies for their programs. ● Providing regular reports on fundraising and external engagement activity. Marketing, Communications & Branding ● Develop and execute strategies to increase the visibility of the college’s athletics programs. ● Ensure consistent use of institutional and athletics branding. ● Create and coordinate promotional content for websites, social media, email, print, and other platforms. ● Work with athletics communications staff to promote accomplishments and stories involving student-athletes and coaches. ● Develop relationships with local media and community organizations. ● Help position athletics as an important component of the college’s overall enrollment, advancement, and community engagement strategy. Qualifications Desired Education, Skills, and Experience: Qualifications Required: ● Bachelor’s degree from an accredited institution. ● Experience in athletics administration, advancement, fundraising, marketing, communications, public relations, development, or a related field. ● Strong written, verbal, interpersonal, and organizational skills. ● Ability to develop and maintain productive relationships with a wide range of constituents. ● Demonstrated ability to manage multiple projects and priorities in a fast-paced environment. ● Ability to work evenings and weekends as required by athletic events and departmental activities. ● Commitment to the educational mission of a small college and the holistic development of student-athletes. Preferred: ● Master’s degree. ● Experience working in intercollegiate athletics. ● Experience with fundraising, alumni relations, corporate sponsorships, or institutional advancement. ● Experience with social media, digital marketing, or strategic communications. ● Familiarity with NCAA and conference rules and regulations. ● Experience with CRM, donor management, or athletics management systems. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities The successful candidate will demonstrate: ● Excellent relationship-building and networking skills. ● Strong fundraising and business-development instincts. ● Exceptional written and verbal communication skills. ● Creativity and initiative in developing new revenue and engagement opportunities. ● Strong attention to detail and follow-through. ● Ability to represent the college professionally and enthusiastically. ● Ability to work independently while collaborating effectively across departments. ● Strong project management and event-planning skills. ● Comfort working in a small-college environment where flexibility and willingness to \"wear multiple hats\" are essential. Work Environment This position operates in a dynamic intercollegiate athletics environment and requires frequent interaction with student-athletes, coaches, alumni, donors, parents, community members, media, and institutional partners. Evening and weekend work is expected based on the athletics schedule, fundraising activities, and special events. Performance Measures Success in this position may be evaluated through: ● Growth in athletics fundraising and sponsorship revenue. ● Increased alumni and donor engagement. ● Development of new corporate and community partnerships. ● Attendance and engagement at athletics events. ● Growth in athletics visibility and digital engagement. ● Successful execution of donor, alumni, and community events. ● Quality and consistency of athletics communications and storytelling. ● Collaboration with Advancement, Communications, Admissions, and other campus partners. About the Role This position is ideal for a relationship-oriented, entrepreneurial athletics professional who enjoys the personal nature of a small-college environment. The successful candidate will be comfortable moving between a donor meeting, a community partnership discussion, a social media campaign, and a Friday-night athletic event—and will understand that building a successful athletics program depends on building strong relationships both inside and outside the campus community Barton College is an equal employment opportunity employer committed to a diverse faculty, staff, and student body and welcomes all applicants. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Any claims of discrimination for Title IX or otherwise should be directed to our Title IX Coordinator, Corey Coley, at P.O. Box 5000, Wilson, NC 27893, or at 252-399-6319 or cocoley@barton.edu. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
