    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/87CB6D0141B0DF4C2F65FFEBD183CE63/jobs/246682": {
      "title": "Assistant Sports Information Director",
      "description": "Assistant Sports Information Director You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Assistant Sports Information Director Barton College - Wilson, NC 27893 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Apply Description The Assistant Sports Information Director (ASID) is responsible for the communications, publicity, statistical management, and digital presentation of approximately 14 of the college's 28 intercollegiate athletic programs. Working under the supervision of the Senior Sports Information Director, the Assistant Sports Information Director serves as the primary communications contact for assigned sports and provides accurate, timely, and engaging coverage of student-athletes, coaches, teams, and athletic events. In addition to traditional sports information responsibilities, this position has significant responsibility for athletics, social media, live streaming and digital production, and ticketing operations. The position plays an important role in increasing the visibility of the athletics department, enhancing the fan experience, and promoting the accomplishments of student-athletes and teams. The successful candidate will be a creative, organized, detail-oriented communications professional who can manage multiple deadlines and events in a fast-paced small-college athletics environment. Essential Responsibilities Sports Information & Communications Serve as the primary Assistant Sports Information Director for approximately 14 of the college's 28 intercollegiate sports. Work under the direction and supervision of the Assistant Athletic Director of Communications to ensure consistency in departmental communications and coverage. Develop and maintain accurate schedules, rosters, statistics, records, results, standings, and historical information for assigned sports. Prepare and distribute game previews, recaps, releases, feature stories, player spotlights, and other athletics communications. Maintain accurate and timely information on the athletics website for assigned sports. Coordinate the collection, verification, and distribution of statistics and results. Maintain historical records and assist with the development of athletics record books and statistical archives. Serve as the primary media contact for assigned sports. Develop and maintain relationships with local, regional, conference, and other media outlets. Coordinate media requests, interviews, credentials, and other media-related activities. Promote student-athlete and team accomplishments through traditional and digital communications. Assist with conference and NCAA statistical and reporting requirements. Coordinate nominations and submissions for conference, regional, and national awards and honors. Assist with postseason and championship communications as assigned. Ensure all published information is accurate, professional, timely, and consistent with institutional standards. Game-Day Statistics & Operations Serve as the primary athletics communications contact for assigned home contests. Coordinate game-day statistical operations, including staffing, equipment, software, and reporting. Operate or oversee statistical software and systems used for assigned sports. Coordinate with coaches, officials, visiting teams, conference personnel, and game-day staff to ensure accurate information and statistics. Distribute results and statistics to appropriate conference, media, institutional, and NCAA outlets. Assist with game-day programs, rosters, announcements, and other promotional materials. Recruit, train, schedule, and supervise student Ticketing Work with the Assistant Athletic Director for Logistics with ticket operations with the athletic department ticketing vendor. Qualifications Bachelor’s degree required from an accredited instittution. Proficiency in Microsoft Office (Outlook, Word, Excel, and PowerPoint); Excellent written and verbal communication skills; strong organizational skills and ability to work independently within the structure of a team. Must be able to exercise good judgment and to maintain a high level of confidentiality, to relate easily to a wide variety of individuals, and to effectively balance and execute multiple priorities. Prior experience with college athletics preferred. Barton College is an equal employment opportunity employer committed to a diverse faculty, staff, and student body and welcomes all applicants. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Any claims of discrimination for Title IX or otherwise should be directed to our Title IX Coordinator, Corey Coley, at P.O. Box 5000, Wilson, NC 27893, or at 252-399-6319 or cocoley@barton.edu . Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/87CB6D0141B0DF4C2F65FFEBD183CE63/jobs/246539": {
      "title": "Director of Housing and Residence Life",
      "description": "Director of Housing and Residence Life You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Director of Housing and Residence Life Barton College - Wilson, NC 27893 Apply Apply Description Reporting to the Executive Director of Student Health Services & Dean of Students, the Director of Residence Life and Chief Judicial Officer is a live-on, full-time, 12-month administrative position with on-call responsibilities. The Director provides strategic vision, leadership, and oversight for the Office of Residence Life and the campus student conduct process. This position plays a critical role in fostering a residential environment that promotes student learning, personal development, accountability, and community engagement. The Director oversees housing operations, residential education, crisis response, and judicial processes while advancing the mission and strategic priorities of Barton College. The Director also serves as a Title IX Deputy Coordinator under the leadership of the Director of Title IX and serves as an administrative resource to students, families, faculty, staff, and campus leadership. Essential Functions Represent Barton College by exemplifying professionalism, respect, and a commitment to student educational development in all interactions. Provide strategic leadership for all residential facilities, including openings, closings, occupancy management, safety protocols, and documentation. Oversee housing assignments, room changes, room selection processes, and maintain accurate residential rosters. Oversee room, furniture, and key inventory systems. Assume fiscal responsibility for the Office of Residence Life, including budget development, management, grants, and fundraising initiatives. Utilize StarRez and Jenzabar EX (or current institutional systems) to administer housing operations, manage residential student data and applications, and provide training to professional staff. Provide oversight of the Barton card access system in collaboration with campus partners. Collaborate with AVI Fresh and other campus partners regarding residential dining processes. Serve on College committees as appointed. Residence Life Staff Supervision and Development Recruit, select, train, supervise, and evaluate professional Residence Life staff and Administrative Support for Campus Life. In collaboration with Coordinators, recruit, select, train, supervise, and evaluate Graduate Assistants and Resident Assistants. Develop and implement a comprehensive Residence Life training program for professional and student staff. Design, maintain, and revise the Residence Life Manual and associated policies and procedures. Lead the development and implementation of departmental goals, objectives, and measurable student learning outcomes consistent with the College mission. Residential Education and Community Development Develop and sustain a residential community that promotes student rights and responsibilities, service learning, leadership development, personal growth, and accountability. Establish measurable operational goals and student learning outcomes for the residential experience. Serve as Chief Judicial Officer, providing oversight and management of the student conduct process. Ensure equitable, educational, and developmentally appropriate conduct practices aligned with institutional policy. Serve as a member of the Title IX leadership team, as directed. Maintain a working knowledge of College regulatory policies, including Clery, Title IX, FERPA, fire safety, and related federal and state regulations. Serve as a liaison between students and College administration, faculty, and staff. Crisis Response and On-Call Responsibilities Maintain regular on-campus presence and availability to residents. Participate in and oversee professional on-call rotation. Coordinate Residence Life crisis response efforts, including campus emergencies, student mental health crises, deaths, injuries, and other critical incidents. Partner with campus safety and senior leadership during emergency situations. Institutional Collaboration Partners with departments across the Division of Student Engagement and the College to advance programs, services, and institutional priorities. Support Student Engagement initiatives and strategic planning efforts. Perform additional duties as assigned by the Executive Director of Student Health Services & Dean of Students. Qualifications Master’s Degree in Student Affairs, Higher Education Leadership, Counseling, or a related field (required). Minimum of three years of professional experience in housing and student life administration with student conduct oversight experience (including Title IX cases). Demonstrated knowledge of student development theory, conduct administration, and residential education best practices. Working knowledge of federal, state, and local regulations impacting higher education housing, including Clery, Title IX, FERPA, and fire safety requirements. Strong written and verbal communication skills with the ability to engage effectively with diverse stakeholders. Ability to handle confidential and sensitive information with discretion. Strong organizational, problem-solving, and strategic planning skills. Ability to work independently in a fast-paced environment with sound judgment and integrity. Proficiency in Microsoft Office, Google Suite, and student information and housing management systems, including StarRez and Jenzabar. Barton College is an equal employment opportunity employer committed to a diverse faculty, staff, and student body and welcomes all applicants. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Any claims of discrimination for Title IX or otherwise should be directed to our Director of Title IX & Campus Relations, Corey Coley, at P.O. Box 5000, Wilson, NC 27893, or at 252-399-6319 or c ocoley@barton.edu. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    }
  },
